{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — A RANGE PAGE: Apparel, Fine Silk, Fine Jewellery, Yoga.
  Aloha's "All Clothing & LOT — build brief for Ivan" and the artboards
  All Clothing - Desktop (1440 x 7450), Interaction & build guide, The LOT /
  design & function — 17 September 2026. Aloha, 18 September: the same
  structure for Fine Silk, Yoga and Fine Jewellery, and the word "Clothing"
  retired in favour of "Apparel" everywhere a visitor reads it. (File and
  class names keep the older word; they are internal, like legacy SKUs.)

  One page per range: header and introduction; the category
  links, sticky below the site header; Made in Lots with its inline "How Lots
  work" disclosure; then a section per category — a rail (number, heading,
  Back to top, a line of copy) beside a three-column grid of garment cards —
  with the Made by Masters feature placed between two of them; onward links;
  then The Register (its own section on the template).

  ONE CARD PER STYLE. The cards are not typed: they are the products of this
  collection grouped by their Style record (hartwick.style). Each card shows
  the Style's HERO Expression — `style.hero_product` when Aloha has chosen
  one, else the first product in collection order that has a photograph —
  and the whole card is ONE link to that product, so the visitor arrives on
  the pictured Expression with its Lot (the product's own hartwick.lot). The
  expression count is the number of products sharing the Style. "LOT [NUMBER]"
  is the design's own placeholder and prints until the hero product carries a
  Lot; nothing is invented.

  A category block names which Style categories it gathers ("Skirt"), and
  may include or exclude Styles by name or by code — "Jasmine Dress" (Dress
  002) sits in Loungewear as the brief proposes. A Style appears once, in the
  first section that claims it. Since 21 September 2026 the card's name is
  the location name (Aloha: "We've returned to the original names … Style
  codes and product IDs stay internal"); the code stays on the style record
  as `code`, so a template written before that date still finds its Style.
  A trailing number (the fine-silk codes) is set in Cutch Resin
  (snippets/ha-style-name).

  ONE CARD PER PRODUCT, where there are no Style records. Fine Silk, Fine
  Jewellery and Yoga have no `hartwick.style` yet, so a category block may
  instead name a COLLECTION (the format or form sub-collection: Classic
  Stoles, Rings …) and the cards are that collection's products, one each,
  in its own order. The card is the same; the count line is simply absent.
  When Style records arrive for those ranges the block can switch back
  without touching the layout.

  BLACK AND WHITE -> COLOUR. Colour originals, `filter: grayscale(1)` at rest,
  colour on hover or focus-within of the card only; no transition under
  reduced motion; on touch screens the photographs are in colour and one tap
  opens the piece (brief, Tablet and mobile) — or, by setting, the Collection
  Index's scroll reveal. Hovering never scrolls or navigates.

  Headings and every product fact are real text and real links: one H1 (All
  Clothing), a section H2 per category, an H3 per Style.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign nav_label = section.settings.nav_label
-%}

<script src="{{ 'ha-collection-categories.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script>
  (function () {
    var reduce = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var a = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-clothing-top]');
      if (!a) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      window.scrollTo({ top: 0, left: 0, behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
      var nav = document.querySelector('.ha-clothing__nav-link');
      if (nav) window.setTimeout(function () { nav.focus({ preventScroll: true }); }, reduce ? 0 : 400);
      if (history.replaceState) history.replaceState(null, '', location.pathname + location.search);
    });
    // The sticky category navigation can run to two lines on a range with
    // long category names (Fine Silk). Its measured height feeds the anchor
    // offsets and the rail's resting point, so nothing hides beneath it.
    function measureNav() {
      var page = document.querySelector('.ha-clothing');
      var nav = document.querySelector('.ha-clothing__nav');
      if (page && nav) page.style.setProperty('--ha-clothing-nav-h', nav.offsetHeight + 'px');
    }
    window.addEventListener('load', measureNav);
    window.addEventListener('resize', measureNav);
    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') measureNav(); else document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', measureNav);
  })();
</script>
{%- paginate collection.products by 250 -%}
<div class="ha-clothing ha-clothing--touch-{{ section.settings.touch }}">

  {%- comment -%} ---------- HEAD ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Aloha, 24 September 2026: every collection page opens on her navy paper
    with Chalk Blue type, the menu transparent over it (header.liquid,
    "Transparent on collection pages"). Chosen per range in "Paper background".
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign head_paper = section.settings.head_paper -%}
  <header class="ha-section ha-clothing__head{% if head_paper %} ha-paper-head{% endif %}" id="clothing-page"{% if head_paper %} style="--ha-paper-bg: url({{ head_paper | image_url: width: 2400 }});"{% endif %}>
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-clothing__head-grid">
      <div>
        <nav class="ha-clothing__crumbs ha-record" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ shop.name }}</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}">{{ section.settings.crumb_collection }}</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>{{ section.settings.crumb_leaf }}</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="ha-clothing__title ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.title | default: collection.title }}</h1>
        {%- if section.settings.back_text != blank -%}
          <a class="ha-clothing__back ha-record" href="{{ section.settings.back_url | default: routes.collections_url }}">{{ section.settings.back_text }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <p class="ha-clothing__intro ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.intro }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- CATEGORY NAVIGATION, sticky ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <nav class="ha-clothing__nav" aria-label="{{ nav_label }}" id="clothing-top">
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-clothing__nav-grid">
      <p class="ha-clothing__nav-label ha-record">{{ nav_label }}</p>
      <ul class="ha-clothing__nav-list" role="list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'category' -%}
            <li><a class="ha-clothing__nav-link ha-record" href="#{{ block.settings.anchor | default: block.id }}">{{ block.settings.heading }}</a></li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </nav>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- MADE IN LOTS ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.lots_line != blank -%}
    <div class="ha-section ha-clothing__lots">
      <div class="ha-wrap ha-clothing__lots-grid">
        <p class="ha-clothing__lots-label ha-identify">{{ section.settings.lots_label }}</p>
        <div class="ha-clothing__lots-body">
          <p class="ha-clothing__lots-line ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.lots_line }}</p>
          {%- comment -%}
            A native disclosure: keyboard-operable, opens below the control on
            every screen, never on hover (brief, 01 / Customer journey). The
            copy is in the page whether open or closed.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <details class="ha-clothing__lots-details">
            <summary class="ha-clothing__lots-toggle ha-record"><span class="ha-clothing__lots-open">{{ section.settings.lots_toggle }}<span aria-hidden="true"> +</span></span><span class="ha-clothing__lots-close">{{ section.settings.lots_toggle }}<span aria-hidden="true"> –</span></span></summary>
            <div class="ha-clothing__lots-more ha-narrate">
              {{ section.settings.lots_more }}
              {%- if section.settings.lots_note != blank -%}<p class="ha-clothing__lots-note ha-record">{{ section.settings.lots_note }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---------- SECTIONS ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign seen = ',' -%}
  {%- assign section_n = 0 -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}

    {%- if block.type == 'feature' -%}
      <section class="ha-section ha-clothing__feature" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        <div class="ha-wrap ha-clothing__feature-grid">
          <div class="ha-clothing__feature-media">
            {%- render 'ha-figure', image: block.settings.image, label: block.settings.image_label, class: 'ha-clothing__feature-figure', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 34vw, 100vw', alt: block.settings.image_alt -%}
          </div>
          <div class="ha-clothing__feature-text">
            {%- if block.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="ha-eyebrow ha-record ha-clothing__feature-eyebrow">{{ block.settings.eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}<h2 class="ha-clothing__feature-heading ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="ha-clothing__feature-body ha-body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.link_text != blank -%}
              <a class="ha-clothing__feature-link ha-record" href="{{ block.settings.link_url | default: '#' }}">{{ block.settings.link_text }}<span class="ha-clothing__corner" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.link_url == blank -%}
              {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note, text: 'The feature link has no destination yet — bind the approved Masters / textile story.' -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    {%- elsif block.type == 'category' -%}
      {%- assign section_n = section_n | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- assign cats = block.settings.categories | downcase | split: ',' -%}
      {%- assign incl = block.settings.include | downcase | split: ',' -%}
      {%- assign excl = block.settings.exclude | downcase | split: ',' -%}
      {%- assign anchor = block.settings.anchor | default: block.id -%}
      <section class="ha-section ha-clothing__cat" id="{{ anchor }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        <div class="ha-wrap ha-clothing__cat-grid">
          <div class="ha-clothing__rail">
            <div class="ha-clothing__rail-inner">
              <p class="ha-clothing__cat-num ha-record">{{ section_n | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</p>
              <h2 class="ha-clothing__cat-heading ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h2>
              {%- comment -%}
                Back to top returns to the head of the page — NOT to the sticky
                navigation. An anchor on a sticky element scrolls to wherever
                that element currently sits, which on a long page is where you
                already are (Ivan, 18 Sept: "doesn't seem to work"). The href
                works without a script; the script makes it smooth and hands
                keyboard focus to the navigation.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <a class="ha-clothing__top ha-record" href="#clothing-page" data-clothing-top>{{ section.settings.top_text }}<span class="ha-clothing__chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
              {%- if block.settings.blurb != blank -%}<p class="ha-clothing__cat-blurb ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.blurb }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          <ul class="ha-clothing__grid" role="list">
            {%- assign cards = 0 -%}
            {%- if block.settings.collection != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%} One card per product of the named collection. {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- for hero in block.settings.collection.products -%}
                {%- assign key = ',' | append: hero.handle | append: ',' -%}
                {%- if seen contains key -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign seen = seen | append: hero.handle | append: ',' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  With no Style record the name is the product title up to its
                  " | " — the part after it is the Expression, which
                  ha-product-fact already reads, so it is not printed twice.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign short_title = hero.title | split: ' | ' | first | strip -%}
                {%- assign sname = hero.metafields.hartwick.style.value.display_name.value | default: hero.metafields.hartwick.style.value.display_name | default: short_title -%}
                {%- assign cards = cards | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- capture expr -%}{%- render 'ha-product-fact', product: hero, field: 'expression' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- assign expr = expr | strip -%}
                {%- assign lot = hero.metafields.hartwick.lot.value.number_roman.value | default: hero.metafields.hartwick.lot.value.number_roman -%}
                {%- assign alt = hero.featured_media.alt | default: sname -%}
                {%- if expr != blank -%}{%- assign alt = sname | append: ', ' | append: expr -%}{%- endif -%}
                <li class="ha-clothing__card">
                  <a class="ha-clothing__link" href="{{ hero.url }}" aria-label="{{ sname | escape }}{% if expr != blank %}, {{ expr | escape }}{% endif %} — {{ section.settings.view_text | escape }}">
                    <figure class="ha-clothing__figure{% unless hero.featured_media %} ha-figure--empty{% endunless %}">
                      {%- if hero.featured_media -%}
                        {{ hero.featured_media.preview_image
                          | image_url: width: 1200
                          | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 26vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200', alt: alt, class: 'ha-clothing__img' }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        <span class="ha-clothing__empty ha-record">{{ section.settings.image_slot_text }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </figure>
                    <h3 class="ha-clothing__name ha-narrate">{%- render 'ha-style-name', name: sname -%}</h3>
                    {%- if expr != blank -%}<p class="ha-clothing__expr ha-narrate">{{ expr }}</p>{%- endif -%}
                    {%- comment -%} Aloha, 25 Sep 2026: "For now, we're not using LOT [Number] on the Collection page … please simply remove it." Kept behind show_lot for when the Lot system returns. {%- endcomment -%}{%- if section.settings.show_lot -%}<p class="ha-clothing__lot ha-record">{% if lot != blank %}{{ section.settings.lot_label }} {{ lot }}{% else %}{{ section.settings.lot_placeholder }}{% endif %}</p>{%- endif -%}
                    <p class="ha-clothing__meta ha-record">{{ section.settings.view_text }}</p>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Two passes. First, every Style this block claims, keyed
              "number|handle" so a plain string sort puts 001 before 002
              before 003 whatever the collection's order. Second, a card per
              key, from the products that share the Style.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign keys = '' -%}
            {%- for product in collection.products -%}
              {%- assign st = product.metafields.hartwick.style.value -%}
              {%- if st == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign key = ',' | append: st.system.handle | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if seen contains key -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign sname = st.display_name.value | default: st.display_name -%}
              {%- assign sname_lc = sname | downcase | strip -%}
              {%- assign scode_lc = st.code.value | default: st.code | downcase | strip -%}
              {%- assign scat = st.category.value | default: st.category | downcase | strip -%}
              {%- assign claim = false -%}
              {%- for c in cats -%}
                {%- assign cs = c | strip -%}
                {%- if cs != blank and cs == scat -%}{%- assign claim = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- for n in incl -%}
                {%- assign ns = n | strip -%}
                {%- if ns != blank and ns == sname_lc -%}{%- assign claim = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if ns != blank and ns == scode_lc -%}{%- assign claim = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- for n in excl -%}
                {%- assign ns = n | strip -%}
                {%- if ns != blank and ns == sname_lc -%}{%- assign claim = false -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if ns != blank and ns == scode_lc -%}{%- assign claim = false -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- unless claim -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
              {%- assign seen = seen | append: st.system.handle | append: ',' -%}
              {%- assign snum = st.number.value | default: st.number | default: '999' -%}
              {%- assign keys = keys | append: snum | append: '|' | append: st.system.handle | append: ',' -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- assign sorted = keys | split: ',' | sort -%}
            {%- for k in sorted -%}
              {%- if k == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign shandle = k | split: '|' | last -%}
              {%- assign st = nil -%}
              {%- assign hero = nil -%}
              {%- assign count = 0 -%}
              {%- for p2 in collection.products -%}
                {%- if p2.metafields.hartwick.style.value.system.handle == shandle -%}
                  {%- if st == nil -%}{%- assign st = p2.metafields.hartwick.style.value -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign count = count | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- if hero == nil and p2.featured_media != blank -%}{%- assign hero = p2 -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if hero == nil -%}{%- assign last_p = p2 -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if st.hero_product.value != blank -%}{%- assign hero = st.hero_product.value -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if hero == nil -%}{%- assign hero = last_p -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign sname = st.display_name.value | default: st.display_name -%}
              {%- assign cards = cards | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- capture expr -%}{%- render 'ha-product-fact', product: hero, field: 'expression' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- assign expr = expr | strip -%}
              {%- assign lot = hero.metafields.hartwick.lot.value.number_roman.value | default: hero.metafields.hartwick.lot.value.number_roman -%}
              {%- assign alt = hero.featured_media.alt | default: sname -%}
              {%- if expr != blank -%}{%- assign alt = sname | append: ', ' | append: expr -%}{%- endif -%}

              <li class="ha-clothing__card">
                <a class="ha-clothing__link" href="{{ hero.url }}" aria-label="{{ sname | escape }}{% if expr != blank %}, {{ expr | escape }}{% endif %} — {{ section.settings.view_text | escape }}">
                  <figure class="ha-clothing__figure{% unless hero.featured_media %} ha-figure--empty{% endunless %}">
                    {%- if hero.featured_media -%}
                      {{ hero.featured_media.preview_image
                        | image_url: width: 1200
                        | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 26vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200', alt: alt, class: 'ha-clothing__img' }}
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="ha-clothing__empty ha-record">{{ section.settings.image_slot_text }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </figure>
                  <h3 class="ha-clothing__name ha-narrate">{%- render 'ha-style-name', name: sname -%}</h3>
                  {%- if expr != blank -%}<p class="ha-clothing__expr ha-narrate">{{ expr }}</p>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- comment -%} Aloha, 25 Sep 2026: "For now, we're not using LOT [Number] on the Collection page … please simply remove it." Kept behind show_lot for when the Lot system returns. {%- endcomment -%}{%- if section.settings.show_lot -%}<p class="ha-clothing__lot ha-record">{% if lot != blank %}{{ section.settings.lot_label }} {{ lot }}{% else %}{{ section.settings.lot_placeholder }}{% endif %}</p>{%- endif -%}
                  <p class="ha-clothing__meta ha-record">{% if count > 1 %}{{ count | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }} {{ section.settings.count_text }} / {% endif %}{{ section.settings.view_text }}</p>
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if cards == 0 -%}
              <li class="ha-clothing__card ha-clothing__card--none"><p class="ha-record">{{ section.settings.none_text }}</p></li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---------- ONWARD ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.onward_label != blank -%}
    <section class="ha-section ha-clothing__onward">
      <div class="ha-wrap ha-clothing__onward-grid">
        <p class="ha-clothing__onward-label ha-record">{{ section.settings.onward_label }}</p>
        <ul class="ha-clothing__onward-list" role="list">
          {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
            {%- assign t = 'onward_' | append: i | append: '_text' -%}
            {%- assign u = 'onward_' | append: i | append: '_url' -%}
            {%- if section.settings[t] != blank -%}
              <li><a class="ha-clothing__onward-link ha-record" href="{{ section.settings[u] | default: '#' }}">{{ section.settings[t] }}</a></li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note,
    text: 'Provisional — Lot references print as the design placeholder until each product carries a Lot; hero photographs are each Style’s first product image until Aloha chooses one on the style record.' -%}
</div>
{%- endpaginate -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Range page",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "A range page — Apparel, Fine Silk, Fine Jewellery or Yoga. Apparel: one card per Style, from this collection's products and their Style records. Ranges without Style records: give each Category block a collection and it lists that collection's products, one card each. Nothing is typed here except headings and copy." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Head" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "head_paper", "label": "Paper background", "info": "Aloha, 24 September 2026: her navy paper behind the head, Chalk Blue type, the menu transparent over it." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_collection", "label": "Breadcrumb: collection", "default": "Collection" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_leaf", "label": "Breadcrumb: this page", "default": "Apparel" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "All Apparel" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "intro", "label": "Introduction", "default": "Apparel in cotton, silk and linen. Find a shape, then explore its cloth, weave and colour." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "back_text", "label": "Back link", "default": "Back to the Collection Index" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "back_url", "label": "Back link URL" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "nav_label", "label": "Navigation label", "default": "Explore apparel" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Made in Lots" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lots_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Made in Lots" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lots_line", "label": "Line", "default": "A Lot is a numbered release of apparel. Each piece belongs to a Lot, with a record of its cloth, making and availability." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lots_toggle", "label": "Disclosure control", "default": "How Lots work" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "lots_more", "label": "Expanded copy", "default": "<p>We release apparel in numbered Lots. The Lot reference connects a piece to its cloth and making. Open a piece to see its Lot details, available sizes and whether it is ready to send or available to pre-order.</p>" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lots_note", "label": "Expanded note", "default": "Dates, quantities and access windows appear only when confirmed." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Cards" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lot_label", "label": "Lot label", "default": "Lot" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_lot", "label": "Show the Lot line on cards", "default": false, "info": "Off (Aloha, 25 September 2026): the Lot system is to be revisited; the line is removed from the cards for this version." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lot_placeholder", "label": "Lot not yet confirmed reads", "default": "Lot [number]" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_text", "label": "Count text", "default": "fabric expressions" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "view_text", "label": "Link text", "default": "View piece" },
